          "usfm": "MAL.2.12",
          "note_ref": "2:12",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Hebrew from the tents of Jacob. The names “Jacob” and “Israel” are often interchanged throughout the Old Testament, referring sometimes to the individual patriarch and sometimes to the nation."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.15",
          "note_ref": "2:15",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Or Didn’t the one Lord make us and preserve our life and breath? or Didn’t the one Lord make her, both flesh and spirit? The meaning of the Hebrew is uncertain."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.16",
          "note_ref": "2:16a",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Hebrew For he hates divorcing."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.16",
          "note_ref": "2:16b",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Hebrew to cover one’s garment with violence."
        }
      ],
